@ [data_design] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Phase3_Inventory_Consistency_Evidence_Revision_Data_Design_2026-07-31.sop

& [JustificationIdentity] is exact
  + [justification_uuid] is 8e791d6b-9eeb-4336-b112-2d2e6056cc6f
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is 4625e9c8-0dbd-4c18-a818-e42df71735bc
  + [status] is justified_unsigned

& [Claim] is narrow
  + replace the current state-inflating consistency vocabulary before any physical scanner or receipt issuer is implemented
  + name the weakest intended evidence NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual and expose it through consistency_evidence
  + retain OsSnapshotProven only as reserved vocabulary and reject it in current receipt validation
  + revise the three affected form profiles while preserving the scanner profile and every unrelated invariant
  + perform the change as a strict two-module pure schema replacement with no migration, dependency, producer, consumer, or effect

& [Support] is direct
  + two non-atomic inventory walks with equal commitments do not prove uninterrupted quiescence
  + change-and-restore can occur between walks
  + change can occur after the second walk before a consumer acts
  + a supervisor may account for its own processes without excluding external writers
  + the current token quiescent_double_inventory therefore carries a stronger ordinary meaning than the intended producer can initially prove
  + documentation beside an overstated serialized token cannot remove that semantic inflation
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual embeds the key limitation in the machine vocabulary itself

& [TimingReason] is ordered
  + the overstatement is already present in shared machine forms and receipt forms
  + the future scanner formation proposes using the overstated value after two equal acquisitions
  + correcting vocabulary before a producer exists avoids persistence, migration, and external-consumer obligations
  + physical scanner work should consume an already honest evidence taxonomy rather than invent a local reinterpretation
  + receipt issuance should consume explicit acquisition support rather than repair the form after the fact

& [AlternativeA_DocumentationOnly] is rejected
  + callers and serialized-data consumers primarily encounter the type, field, and token
  + quiescent remains a positive world-state implication even when prose later narrows it
  + static and schema-level honesty is stronger than relying on every consumer to discover a caveat

& [AlternativeB_KeepConsistencyClassRenameOnlyVariant] is rejected
  + ConsistencyClass still sounds like a classification of state rather than a grade of support
  + TopologyReceipt.consistency would still invite consumers to read the label as a direct property of the candidate
  + type and field must both expose their evidentiary role

& [AlternativeC_UseRepeatedInventoryEqual] is rejected
  + it removes quiescence but leaves atomic or snapshot interpretation unstated
  + non-atomicity is the central limitation and belongs in the weakest public token

& [AlternativeD_RemoveOsSnapshotProven] is rejected for this revision
  + predecessor design already delineates a stronger snapshot evidence point
  + retaining the closed token preserves the intended lattice without granting receipt admissibility
  + exact rejection at consistency_evidence makes the missing provenance operationally visible

& [AlternativeE_AdmitOsSnapshotProvenNow] is rejected
  + current data has no snapshot primitive, identity, producer, view, lifetime, or acquisition binding
  + enum selection cannot stand in for those missing provenance edges
  + admission would repeat the exact evidence inflation this revision repairs

& [AlternativeF_AddSupervisorQuiescedGrade] is deferred
  + supervisor-owned process shutdown does not automatically exclude external writers
  + exact enforcement, observation, failure, and consumer semantics are not mature
  + speculative taxonomy growth would make the revision harder to verify and easier to misuse

& [AlternativeG_MigrateLegacyJSON] is rejected
  + no live producer or persisted consumer is evidenced
  + rewriting quiescent_double_inventory to non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal would silently assign a new meaning to old bytes
  + explicit decode and compile failure forces a conscious semantic update

& [AlternativeH_WaitForPhysicalScanner] is rejected
  + it would couple a pure vocabulary correction to handles, traversal, acquisition order, completeness, and physical fixtures
  + those effects remain separately locked
  + the form boundary is independently testable and should be settled before physical code depends on it

& [Counterargument] is considered
  + the old enum is currently only a pure form and no producer yet releases it
  + therefore immediate operational harm is limited
  + but shared public vocabulary is itself an authority surface, and leaving the inflated term in place would cause future code, tests, and documentation to build around the wrong concept
  + pre-producer correction is the lowest-cost and highest-integrity point to act

& [TwoSignatureReason] is explicit
  + phase3_evidence.rs and topology_forms.rs are governed by distinct existing canonical specifications and satisfaction signatures
  + one coordinating revision source is appropriate because the type and its receipt field must change atomically in source meaning
  + one undifferentiated replacement signature would obscure which prior authority and module scope it supersedes
  + two scoped replacement signatures under one canonical revision preserve atomic coordination and module-specific lineage
  + the machine-forms signature supersedes ae44deed-29c7-4a6a-96d1-1a0091539575 only for the selected machine-forms meaning
  + the topology-forms signature supersedes 0e2cfacb-8659-41c2-b804-0eb1b49ff5b2 only for the selected topology-forms meaning
  + unchanged historical proofs remain immutable and inspectable

& [Confidence] is high inside the pure boundary
  + seven independent folds converge without material question
  + twenty-four source constraints reapply without conflict
  + data identity, ownership, cardinality, representation, validation, fault, version, and provenance models close
  + the exact code surface is already identified and requires no new type payload, collection, dependency, or effect
  + remaining uncertainty belongs to future physical acquisition and issuance, which this revision excludes

& [Risk] is explicit
  + highest risk is treating a structurally valid evidence label as self-proving support
  + next risk is silently accepting the old token or field through serde compatibility
  + next risk is admitting OsSnapshotProven because the enum structurally validates it
  + next risk is widening the revision into physical acquisition or receipt issuance
  + documentation nonclaims, strict negative fixtures, static scans, exact receipt rejection, two scoped signatures, and production-diff limits mitigate those risks

& [InvalidationCondition] is exact
  + raw source or SJS input manifest drift
  + either affected predecessor authority is omitted or misidentified
  + old type, variant, field, token, or profile remains accepted
  + snapshot value succeeds in TopologyReceipt 0.3
  + supplied reconciliation is treated as actual repeated acquisition proof
  + scanner profile changes
  + unrelated receipt invariant changes
  + migration, alias, default, conversion, extra variant, producer, consumer, dependency, unsafe, platform call, filesystem, clock, effect, stale evidence, or failed proof appears

& [Decision] is proceed only through complete replacement authority
  + canonicalize one coordinated revision with two exact scoped replacement signatures
  + implement only the exact two-module pure schema delta and governed support after both signatures validate
  + preserve physical scanning, acquisition, issuance, consumption, admission, mutation, seal, cleanup, promotion, neural, distributed, FPGA, and every effect boundary as absent
